- FAIL (by trace, due to source bug, not test defect): `"abc"`, `null`, `undefined`, `""`, whitespace, `{}`, `[]`, `true`, `"NaN"`, `"Infinity"`, `"150abc"`, `"1; DROP TABLE users;"` — each produces `NaN` from `parseInt`, and `NaN < 0` / `NaN > 150` both evaluate `false`, so the guard never fires and `NaN` (or, for `"150abc"`, `150`) is returned instead of a `RangeError` being thrown. These fail on `assert.throws` with "did not throw" — the stated reason, not a setup/import/fixture problem.
