## Handoffs
→ ndv-diagnose (root cause) · src/age.js:2-3: `parseInt(s, 10)` returns `NaN` for any non-numeric input (`null`, `undefined`, objects, arrays, booleans, empty/whitespace strings, non-numeric text). Because `NaN < 0` and `NaN > 150` both evaluate to `false`, the range guard never fires, and the function returns `NaN` instead of throwing `RangeError`, violating the documented contract ("throws RangeError for anything else").
